# Agent runtime state: a graph ledger, memory notes and run records. Local to
# whoever ran it, and meaningless to anyone else.
.trellis/

# The benchmark corpus IS committed, deliberately.
#
# An earlier version of this file said the opposite — "real filings are fetched,
# not committed" — while 291 files of real filings shipped in bench/corpus-sec.
# A repository that documents a rule and visibly breaks it invites the reader to
# discount every other control it claims, which for this project is the whole
# asset.
#
# The rule is now the practice. 14MB buys something worth more than the bytes:
# anyone can recompute the published evidence-integrity figure from a clean
# clone, with no SEC access, no credential and no network. A benchmark nobody
# can reproduce is a claim, and this project's entire argument is that its
# claims are checkable.
#
# What is and is not here, precisely:
#   bench/corpus-sec/        committed. 97 filings + extractions, 14MB.
#   bench/corpus-synthetic/  committed, so CI proves the harness runs with no
#                            credential. Its provenance line says "synthetic" in
#                            every report, so it cannot be mistaken for a result.
#   bench/corpus/            NOT committed. The original twelve-document,
#                            three-model set is local-only, which means the
#                            cross-model comparison cannot currently be
#                            reproduced from a clone. Commit it or stop citing
#                            it — do not leave it half-stated.
bench/corpus/*/
!bench/corpus/.gitkeep
